; MOCHI archive descriptor, schema version 0 (FROZEN with draft 2; ratification items R1, R2).
; Decision: spec Annex B.2 D12.
;
; Stored as the payload of one skippable frame of kind ARCHIVE_DESCRIPTOR
; (0x184D2A57) at offset 0, written once at creation and never rewritten.
; Every commit references it (commit v1 key 10). A descriptor frame at any
; other offset is invalid. Encoding: the deterministic-CBOR subset of Annex
; B.1 D2. The CBOR-native envelope (D11) is keys 0, 1, and 4, plus the frame
; kind and frame length. Identity is the archive ID.
;
; This file is complete and standalone: every rule it uses is defined here.
;
; Rules CDDL cannot state, checked by the code (R3 section 7 lists them):
;   * features are strictly increasing (ENVELOPE_INVALID) and every entry is
;     known (UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE); the Encrypted feature (1) cannot be
;     combined with the TAR-compatible constraint (DESCRIPTOR_INVALID);
;   * the draft identifier is null (a ratified 1.0 archive). A number is a
;     pre-1.0 draft: every command but `migrate` refuses it
;     (UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE), `migrate` reads draft 2 only, and no build reads
;     another number. The wire generation is 2;
;   * the redundancy suite is known (UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE).
;
; The descriptor holds only creation-time facts. It never locates key
; envelopes (§14.3: commits do), and it never changes. Changing a
; creation-time constraint, including adopting the Encrypted profile, means
; writing a new archive (D12).

descriptor = {
  0: 0,                       ; descriptor schema version
  1: archive-id,
  2: 2,                       ; wire generation: MOCHI2 (Annex B.1 D1)
  3: draft,
  4: features,                ; required features; Core = []; unknown entry => refuse
  5: constraints,
  ? 6: declared-limits,       ; present ONLY when the writer opted into limits above reader defaults (D10.8)
}

; Draft identifier. Null = a ratified 1.0 archive, which is all a 1.0 writer
; writes. A number is a pre-1.0 draft: 2 = the layout frozen at G12 (1 was the
; pre-freeze batch). The two layouts differ in this value alone (and what
; hashes it). Archives from before the batches carry no descriptor and are
; rejected as legacy drafts (§26).
draft = uint / null

constraints = {
  0: bool,                    ; TAR-compatible profile (Annex B.1 D4), fixed at creation
  ? 1: redundancy,            ; Redundancy profile (Annex B.2.11 D21), fixed at creation; absent = none
}

; The recovery record: every commit writes parity frames laid out from
; these (D21; ratification artifact R6). An unknown suite => refuse
; (UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE); a percentage outside 1..100 => DESCRIPTOR_INVALID.
redundancy = {
  0: uint,                    ; suite: 1 = Cauchy Reed-Solomon over GF(2^8), layout rule v0
  1: 1..100,                  ; parity percentage r
}

; Advisory only. Readers MUST NOT raise their own limits from these values.
; A reader whose limits are lower reports LIMIT_EXCEEDED, naming the
; declared value, and requires an explicit user setting to proceed.
declared-limits = {
  0: uint,                    ; max skippable payload the writer used
  1: uint,                    ; max CBOR items per record
  2: uint,                    ; max catalog image length
}

archive-id = bstr .size 32
features = [* uint]           ; strictly increasing
